const string GS_ORIGIN_NYROND  = "You either were born in the Kingdom of Nyrond, or have lived here for many years. Its feudal ways come naturally to you and, whether you chafe against it or not, a place in society has been decided for you. One's trade is decided more by their upbringing than anything, although the devastating Greyhawk Wars and their aftershocks have given many the opportunity to change their stars.\n\nCommoners rarely suffer oppression, but are nevertheless beneath the mastery of knightly and dignified noble houses. A council of a dozen powerful churches dominate the realm, although none are as powerful as the Church of Heironeous. Everyone aspires to those celestial virtues, but many fall short. The Greyhawk Wars have tested the country more than anything else in its history; it is no secret that King Archbold III struggles to rebuild the kingdom after its incredible losses, and the past years have been marked with borderline-ruinous taxes and the horrors of war.\n\nPlayers taking this background should be comfortable with learning the lore quickly on their feet, if they do not know it already.";

const string GS_ORIGIN_FOREIGN = "From the nearest to the farthest corners of the Flanaess, you have come to Nyrond to seek glory, fortune, or something else entirely, and that pursuit has taken you here to Midmeadow. You may have even just immigrated to Nyrond, and are so new a citizen that many of its customs remain strange to you.\n\nForeigners appreciate many of the same legal protections as Nyrond's commoners, as the kingdom still espouses the virtues of justice. However, many may find their social advancement stunted in some way so long as they remain foreigners; the higher they go, the stronger the pressure to formally become citizens of Nyrond.\n\nThis is the recommended background for players unfamiliar with Greyhawk or the Kingdom of Nyrond; beyond the borders of this realm, which castle or village one hails from is of little consequence to the general immersion of others.";
